{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792577108,"nonce":"JL9v0ki+eWFp5qSO2xjcyDS7KnI=","metadata":{"github-url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/30","origin":"github","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:id":"I_kwDOUJip488AAAABYyaxaw","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:labels":"","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:number":"30","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:status":"open","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:text":"7b2234db22805e492c2be8ecf392d6a666862901782dbd044df1b15764dd231b","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:title":"bridge: keep a bridge's label namespaces off the forge","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/30"},"title":"bridge: keep a bridge's label namespaces off the forge","message":"Prerequisite for ADR 0001 item 1. Today the git-bug fork sends every label it doesn't translate to the forge as a label: `status:`, `prio:`, `est:`, `sprint:` and `mod:` reach GitHub as labels, even when git-board writes them to the Project. The fork has no way to keep a label namespace off a forge.\n\n## What to build (fork, `bridge-sync`)\n- A per-bridge key listing namespaces kept off the forge, for example `git config git-bug.bridge.\u003cname\u003e.held status,prio,est,sprint,mod`. git-board writes it into each clone, as it writes `assignees`, `kinds` and `sprints`, and only with `[github-project]` `write = true`.\n- A held namespace is outside the forge's label set on both sides:\n  - it is never sent;\n  - its absence on the forge is never read as a removal;\n  - the label set recorded as last seen leaves it out.\n  The fork already does this for assignees (`labeled` in `bridge/core/syncassignees.go`).\n- Clean-up: a held label already on a forge issue comes off at the next sync, and the dry run lists it.\n- Issues not on the Project: hold nothing back for them, or git-board adds them to the Project first (ADR item 1).\n\n## Notes\n- native-fields left `sprint:` labels going to GitHub on purpose, because co2's Project writes are off. This key is how git-board would hold them back once it writes the Project.\n- Live tests on scratch forges only (guilbep/git-bug-sync-test, guilbep/git-board-test with Project 1).","files":null}]}